{{About|the monster and associated game content}}
[[File:Harbinger.png|thumb|right|400px|A Harbinger]]
'''Harbingers''' are a type of [[monster]]s that cannot be harmed directly. Harbingers summon enemies to fight the player while empowering them in different ways, and they can only be harmed by killing their minions. Harbingers can drop [[Shard|currency shards]], for both ones seen in Wraeclast as well as their own exclusive currency.

Harbingers do not spawn naturally in [[maps]] unlike most other forms of [[Extra Content]]. They can be encountered via the [[Ominous Arrival]] or Additional Harbinger Chance [[Atlas Passive Skill Tree|Atlas passive skills]], using the Harbinger [[map device]] crafting option, in [[Commander_Kirac|Kirac]]'s Atlas missions, in Harbinger nodes in the [[Azurite Mine]], or by using a {{il|Harbinger Scarab}}.

They were introduced to the game as a feature of the [[Harbinger league]].

==Abilities==
Harbingers are invulnerable enemies that cannot be damaged directly and instead defeated by continuously defeating waves of summoned monsters. Harbingers can use a skill similar to {{il|Convocation}} regularly to teleport these monsters. Harbingers can also summon Obelisks which can attack players directly, create a {{stl|Proximity Shield}}, or have buff or debuff aura effects.

Harbingers can also use a variety of spells depending on their variant. These skills include recoloured versions of skills like {{il|Flame Dash}} or {{il|Ball Lightning}}, cast buffs or debuff skills, or cause effects on their summoned monsters such as creating a {{il|Righteous Fire}}-like degeneration aura around a monster.

Some Harbingers can use [[aura]] skills or use certain [[Hex]]es or [[Mark]]s as an aura.
